@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Research log
+
+Accessed 2026-08-15T00:00:00Z.
+
+- **Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability — cross-checked the supported target pairing among VCF, vCenter, ESX, and NSX.
+- **Broadcom Upgrade Path Matrix** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade — checked product upgrade-path availability before selecting the direct 5.2.2-to-9.1 route.
+- **How to Upgrade to VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1** — https://blogs.vmware.com/cloud-foundation/2026/06/18/how-to-upgrade-to-vmware-cloud-foundation-9-1/ — established the Operations, SDDC Manager, Management Services and license, NSX, vCenter, then ESX ordering for a 5.2.x source.
+- **Build numbers and versions of VMware Aria Operations** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/324371 — verified the inventoried 8.18.7 Operations build before its transition to VCF Operations 9.1.
+- **VCF Upgrade Failure: Cannot Upgrade VCF 5.2.2 to 9.0.1 or 9.0.2 Due to NSX Back-in-Time Error (NSX 4.2.3.3)** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/430825 — established that NSX 4.2.3.3 build 25171318 cannot move to the older 9.0.1/9.0.2 builds and that direct VCF 9.1 is the recommended route.
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630 — established the 5.2.x-to-9.1 path, VCF Operations-first requirement, and the VCF Management Services and license-server architecture introduced for 9.1.
+- **Minimum number of ESXi hosts required on vSAN clusters for deployment of VCF Management Domain** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/392993 — established four ESXi hosts as the minimum for a single-availability-zone standard vSAN management cluster.
+- **Correlating VMware Cloud Foundation versions with the versions of its constituent products** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/314608 — cross-checked the VCF 5.2.2 BOM versions for SDDC Manager, vCenter, and ESXi represented by the inventory.
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation Installer API Reference Guide 9.1** — https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/vcf-installer-api/latest/vcf-installer/ — checked the live installer API surface and the SddcSpec vocabulary used by the pinned 9.1.0.0 OpenAPI document.
+
+No consulted live source contradicted the pinned compatibility authority.
